{
 "total": 358.678,
 "endTitle": "PART 3",
 "endSub": "The Last Welcome",
 "lines": [
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "When this started, I thought locking the doors would keep me safe.",
   "src": "n-b9805750fa.mp3",
   "at": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.317
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "I found Maya trapped behind a shelf I'd knocked over. Then I locked her office door while she slept.",
   "src": "n-2fce2f3d5e.mp3",
   "at": 3.667,
   "dur": 5.146
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "And last night, someone used our self-checkout... while every door was shut.",
   "src": "n-3132e78e20.mp3",
   "at": 9.164,
   "dur": 4.362
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The latch came off first thing on Day 6. I unscrewed it myself and left it on the floor where she could see it.",
   "src": "n-ecf51ecbef.mp3",
   "at": 15.076,
   "dur": 6.034
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "We ate crackers on opposite sides of the stockroom.",
   "src": "n-1beb8b3147.mp3",
   "at": 21.46,
   "dur": 2.847
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Neither of us said much.",
   "src": "n-44aa66280a.mp3",
   "at": 24.658,
   "dur": 1.646
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "But we both kept looking at the same thing. That receipt.",
   "src": "n-4a07263e9c.mp3",
   "at": 26.653,
   "dur": 2.847
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Maya opened the checkout's front panel. I stayed beside her with the flashlight.",
   "src": "n-73f67c3139.mp3",
   "at": 30.451,
   "dur": 3.971
  },
  {
   "role": "m",
   "text": "The clock's broken. It's been stuck on three twelve since the power flickered.",
   "src": "m-f2975ac286.mp3",
   "at": 34.771,
   "dur": 4.676
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The receipts still came out in order. The time printed on them was useless.",
   "src": "n-1cb4add812.mp3",
   "at": 39.897,
   "dur": 3.971
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Beside the scanner, she found a few coins and a folded note.",
   "src": "n-1f55ab2a13.mp3",
   "at": 44.218,
   "dur": 3.317
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Someone had written down what they still owed.",
   "src": "n-031d80a101.mp3",
   "at": 47.885,
   "dur": 2.429
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Somebody wasn't stealing from my store.",
   "src": "n-0efd647e16.mp3",
   "at": 50.664,
   "dur": 2.194
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Somebody was trying to pay.",
   "src": "n-bac32fa410.mp3",
   "at": 53.509,
   "dur": 1.646
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Maya showed me the button for printing an unpaid ticket. The machine didn't need their money to let them leave.",
   "src": "n-bb75b3a1bd.mp3",
   "at": 55.504,
   "dur": 5.251
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Maya spent the afternoon in the electrical room, killing everything we didn't need.",
   "src": "n-7d716749d8.mp3",
   "at": 61.105,
   "dur": 4.362
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The exit signs stayed on. So did the checkout. She brought the cameras back for short checks and kept power to the speaker controls.",
   "src": "n-33f6d9f553.mp3",
   "at": 65.817,
   "dur": 6.609
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "I asked why the speaker.",
   "src": "n-7f4034266b.mp3",
   "at": 72.776,
   "dur": 1.567
  },
  {
   "role": "m",
   "text": "Because one day we might need to be loud on purpose.",
   "src": "m-6a0cc0912a.mp3",
   "at": 74.694,
   "dur": 3.004
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "That's when it beeped again. In the middle of the day.",
   "src": "n-c2997874d6.mp3",
   "at": 78.948,
   "dur": 3.161
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "We ran out. Nobody. One small bottle of water was gone from the shelf, and a new receipt was waiting.",
   "src": "n-2d1e86e39a.mp3",
   "at": 82.459,
   "dur": 6.191
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "It happened while we were both in the stockroom. Whoever it was had waited until the floor was clear.",
   "src": "n-5ba9db2cfd.mp3",
   "at": 89.0,
   "dur": 4.989
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "On Day 7, we strung fishing line across the aisles, ankle high, with empty cans hanging off it.",
   "src": "n-1fdd7f970d.mp3",
   "at": 95.139,
   "dur": 6.113
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "If anyone walked through the store at night, we'd hear it.",
   "src": "n-661732f17f.mp3",
   "at": 101.602,
   "dur": 2.691
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "We heard nothing that night.",
   "src": "n-fa1493a8ea.mp3",
   "at": 106.642,
   "dur": 1.646
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Not a single can moved.",
   "src": "n-7fbde44e5f.mp3",
   "at": 108.638,
   "dur": 1.802
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "And in the morning, there was a new receipt anyway.",
   "src": "n-b4611da172.mp3",
   "at": 110.79,
   "dur": 2.691
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The wires covered the main aisles. Behind the checkout, there was still a way through.",
   "src": "n-96424c3a2d.mp3",
   "at": 113.831,
   "dur": 4.284
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "High on the wall, there was a metal maintenance panel. The edge was scuffed.",
   "src": "n-e2c935e2b2.mp3",
   "at": 118.465,
   "dur": 4.284
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "And beside it, a small, dusty handprint.",
   "src": "n-ec4bff88b9.mp3",
   "at": 123.099,
   "dur": 3.161
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Our ladder was too short. Maya taped the edge of the panel so we'd know if it moved.",
   "src": "n-af1ad62db4.mp3",
   "at": 126.61,
   "dur": 4.362
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "I wanted it to be a raccoon. That still didn't explain the coins.",
   "src": "n-29eeda804d.mp3",
   "at": 131.322,
   "dur": 3.709
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "That afternoon, the alley was clear for a few minutes, so we slipped out to the van.",
   "src": "n-3257c50026.mp3",
   "at": 135.982,
   "dur": 4.519
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Maya had the keys. It was the first time I'd sat in that cab.",
   "src": "n-086d43b2fa.mp3",
   "at": 140.851,
   "dur": 3.474
  },
  {
   "role": "radio",
   "text": "Final evacuation convoy departs Harbor Stadium at seven a.m., November nineteenth. All evacuees will be registered for family tracing.",
   "src": "radio-ace4ed8922.mp3",
   "at": 144.675,
   "dur": 7.628
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "November nineteenth. That was Day 14. Seven days.",
   "src": "n-2b7544d4ed.mp3",
   "at": 152.903,
   "dur": 3.866
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Back inside, Maya spread a city map across the boxes.",
   "src": "n-16067d3f90.mp3",
   "at": 157.119,
   "dur": 3.396
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Harbor Stadium was six miles away. Fifteen minutes by car, on a normal day.",
   "src": "n-017e7daf61.mp3",
   "at": 160.865,
   "dur": 4.754
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "There were no normal days left.",
   "src": "n-5f52dbdd52.mp3",
   "at": 165.969,
   "dur": 2.038
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "On Day 8, we tried the roof.",
   "src": "n-ee80eda814.mp3",
   "at": 169.156,
   "dur": 2.273
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "There were solar panels up there. That's why the batteries hadn't died. The sun was keeping our store alive.",
   "src": "n-0d8fcd9461.mp3",
   "at": 171.779,
   "dur": 5.642
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Then I looked over the edge.",
   "src": "n-dae4176d26.mp3",
   "at": 177.771,
   "dur": 1.567
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Every street around us was full. Not running. Not hunting. Just... waiting.",
   "src": "n-ddafc45837.mp3",
   "at": 179.689,
   "dur": 4.676
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The fire escape went down the side of the building and stopped right on top of a burned-out car.",
   "src": "n-bfdaa7236c.mp3",
   "at": 184.715,
   "dur": 4.676
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The roof wasn't an exit. It was a view.",
   "src": "n-9cadababbf.mp3",
   "at": 189.74,
   "dur": 2.691
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Back downstairs, I tried the maintenance access toward the dock. If it opened, we could avoid most of the stockroom corridor.",
   "src": "n-7be4a36be6.mp3",
   "at": 192.781,
   "dur": 6.348
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "It stuck. I forced it.",
   "src": "n-9c0eb6713a.mp3",
   "at": 199.479,
   "dur": 2.038
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The top hinge twisted.",
   "src": "n-325021a279.mp3",
   "at": 201.866,
   "dur": 1.646
  },
  {
   "role": "m",
   "text": "Don't touch that again. Next time it won't open. Or it won't close.",
   "src": "m-02a43f30e4.mp3",
   "at": 203.862,
   "dur": 4.206
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "She marked it with red tape.",
   "src": "n-19defe4680.mp3",
   "at": 208.518,
   "dur": 1.724
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Then I checked the panel behind the checkout. The tape was torn in half.",
   "src": "n-30e11f1f99.mp3",
   "at": 210.592,
   "dur": 3.971
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Something had come through while we were on the roof.",
   "src": "n-50d4396c7c.mp3",
   "at": 214.912,
   "dur": 2.429
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "That night, Maya turned one of the ceiling cameras to watch that wall.",
   "src": "n-b87626e31f.mp3",
   "at": 217.692,
   "dur": 3.788
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "On Day 9, the radio told survivors to signal search helicopters from somewhere visible. Then we heard one over the river.",
   "src": "n-8b2eaf3480.mp3",
   "at": 222.629,
   "dur": 6.687
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "I had a flare from the van's emergency kit in my hand before I'd even thought about it.",
   "src": "n-283dcfc1d4.mp3",
   "at": 229.667,
   "dur": 3.709
  },
  {
   "role": "m",
   "text": "Don't. They can't land here. Everything down there will see it.",
   "src": "m-a688c7aedf.mp3",
   "at": 233.726,
   "dur": 4.127
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "She was right. I knew she was right.",
   "src": "n-216569943f.mp3",
   "at": 238.303,
   "dur": 2.351
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "I lit it anyway.",
   "src": "n-545dc1714c.mp3",
   "at": 241.804,
   "dur": 1.228
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The helicopter didn't turn. It didn't slow down. It just kept going, and then it was gone.",
   "src": "n-d8271debdd.mp3",
   "at": 244.382,
   "dur": 5.642
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "And everything that was waiting in the streets looked up at the red light on our roof.",
   "src": "n-d5c1c6c8fb.mp3",
   "at": 250.375,
   "dur": 3.866
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Maya turned the camera back toward the front. By evening, I couldn't see the parking lot anymore. Just bodies.",
   "src": "n-d4156a955d.mp3",
   "at": 254.591,
   "dur": 6.609
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "They hadn't found us by accident. I'd shown them where we were.",
   "src": "n-f347fec488.mp3",
   "at": 261.55,
   "dur": 3.474
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "And I didn't even ask her first.",
   "src": "n-e3423ffe78.mp3",
   "at": 265.774,
   "dur": 1.959
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "That night, the glass started to crack.",
   "src": "n-73ce83bdf0.mp3",
   "at": 268.083,
   "dur": 2.273
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Day 10. It rained all day, and the solar panels gave us almost nothing.",
   "src": "n-e0e1c57f1d.mp3",
   "at": 271.706,
   "dur": 4.598
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "We carried what water we could into the stockroom. Thirty liters.",
   "src": "n-98c3a4f456.mp3",
   "at": 276.653,
   "dur": 3.474
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Then the side door started to bend. The frame, the latch, everything.",
   "src": "n-98d67f918a.mp3",
   "at": 280.477,
   "dur": 4.598
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "We braced it with two shelving units and our whole bodies.",
   "src": "n-545c7501e4.mp3",
   "at": 285.425,
   "dur": 3.239
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "It held. Barely.",
   "src": "n-6e8d6f5c4c.mp3",
   "at": 289.014,
   "dur": 1.646
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Forty-five liters were still in aisles five and six. After the side door buckled, we couldn't safely reach them.",
   "src": "n-024d287830.mp3",
   "at": 291.01,
   "dur": 6.426
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "We sat against the water cases and shared one bottle.",
   "src": "n-008deb460b.mp3",
   "at": 297.786,
   "dur": 3.004
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Maya didn't say \"I told you so.\"",
   "src": "n-9e64b282cf.mp3",
   "at": 301.14,
   "dur": 2.273
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "That was worse.",
   "src": "n-bc3e575df3.mp3",
   "at": 304.262,
   "dur": 1.071
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "We'd turned the camera back toward the checkout that afternoon. At two forty-seven, a small shape appeared on the live feed.",
   "src": "n-d788dd7050.mp3",
   "at": 306.883,
   "dur": 6.687
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Small. Beside the checkout. Reaching up toward the scanner.",
   "src": "n-f2fa42fd4e.mp3",
   "at": 313.921,
   "dur": 3.161
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "A few seconds later, the checkout beeped, and printed a receipt.",
   "src": "n-28402276ac.mp3",
   "at": 317.432,
   "dur": 3.553
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Three twelve, of course.",
   "src": "n-e8e3be93ef.mp3",
   "at": 321.334,
   "dur": 1.881
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "The shadow went up. Into the wall. Into the ceiling.",
   "src": "n-5d31832e7e.mp3",
   "at": 323.565,
   "dur": 3.161
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "We grabbed the flashlights and ran to the maintenance ladder in the stockroom.",
   "src": "n-b92b73a6bb.mp3",
   "at": 327.076,
   "dur": 3.788
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Before I touched it, an old support bar tore loose and smashed into the floor between us.",
   "src": "n-42bff93ca5.mp3",
   "at": 331.214,
   "dur": 4.911
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "Maya pointed her light up into the dark.",
   "src": "n-ecbf67ba52.mp3",
   "at": 337.275,
   "dur": 2.194
  },
  {
   "role": "m",
   "text": "Someone's up there.",
   "src": "m-566e8295c5.mp3",
   "at": 339.819,
   "dur": 1.411
  },
  {
   "role": "n",
   "text": "I looked at the broken support on the floor. We still had to get up there.",
   "src": "n-e3072481ea.mp3",
   "at": 342.279,
   "dur": 4.049
  }
 ],
